ASoC: sunxi: add the H713 MSP audio DSP driver

HDMI audio on the H713 never touches the CPU. The receiver hands its I2S
to a Trident "MSP" DSP on the demodulator bus at 0x0614xxxx; the DSP runs
it through a module graph and pushes it out of I2SOUT1 into the codec's
I2S window. On a stock system nothing on the ARM owns that block either:
snd_alsa_trid.ko has no clk_get, no reset_control_* and no pm_runtime
(doku/nachtlog/S17), sunxi_tvtop powers the island and libmspdriver.so
drives the mailbox from user space. Mainline has neither, so this driver
does all of it in one place.

What it does, in the order measured on a HY310 on 08.09.2026 and written
down in doku/101-plan-audio-treiber.md section 3:

  island: bus-demod gate off and reset asserted, 10 ms; reset released
  and gate on, 20 ms -- without that the whole Trident front-end space
  reads zero (S17 section 2c); TVFE router 0x06700000 := 0x003003FF,
  12 ms; audio top 0x0614A000 |= 0x700, 0x0614A00C := (old & 0xFF000000)
  | 0x001A5E00, then |= 0x01000000; 300 ms for the DSP's ROM boot.

  mailbox: a write waits for busy bit 4 in +0x00 and puts addr<<16 | val
  into +0x0C; a read puts addr<<16 into +0x10 and is finished when ready
  bit 5 is set and bit 31 of +0x10 is clear, after the outstanding sign
  has been seen once. Accepting an answer earlier is what shifted every
  answer by one register and hung the download (S16 19:30).

  patch: h713/msp-patch.bin, 724 pairs in eight MSPM blocks. A block is
  written without a single read, then exactly one read of 0x00EE at the
  block boundary wakes the monitor, then the next block. Without those
  reads the DSP stays in download mode; with reads inside a block the
  latch words are lost. The wake-up protocol took the patch in 20 of 20
  runs, 15 ms each (S16 20:15). Success is 0x80FF = 1, 0x0001 = 0x0C19.

  graph: path 0xC1 "HDMI2PCM_TO_SPEAKER" without DELAY1 (S23 section
  4.4, S16 18:00). DELAY1 is not broken, it is off and would need the
  DRAM loop of S26; the HY310 runs it with spk_delay = 0, so the bypass
  costs the 2 ms of lip sync stock spends and nothing else.

  card: snd_card "hy310hdmi" / "HY310 HDMI Audio" with three controls
  and no PCM device -- "HDMI Audio Switch" (I2SIN1 enable, 0x0012 bit
  15), "HDMI Playback Volume" (0..400 = -100..0 dB in quarter steps,
  written into 0x0052/0x0053 bits 15:6 as two's complement; 0xFB00 was
  measured as -4.9 dB) and "HDMI Mute Switch" (0x0050/0x0051 = 0x8000).

  sysfs state/levels/reset/compressed and debugfs h713-msp/status.
  "levels" hangs QPEAK on I2SIN1.out0/out1 and reads 0x00B2/0x00B3 (S25
  section 8); "compressed" decodes 0x800A bit 7 and bit 5 (S27 4.1).

  self-healing: every mailbox timeout puts the driver into "error",
  resets the island and builds everything again, at most three times.
  The island reset revived the DSP in 65 of 65 wedged runs (S16 18:20);
  after three failures a write to sysfs "reset" is the way back.

The TVFE router word at 0x06700000 lies inside the second reg entry of
tvtop@5700000. It is taken as a syscon phandle rather than as a register
range of this node, so the sharing is written down in the device tree
instead of hidden; CONFIG_SUNXI_TVTOP is off in this tree, and if it is
ever turned on the router and the demod reset belong to it.

The three audio rates are set through the clock API -- audio-cpu 400
MHz, audio-umac and audio-ihb 200 MHz, the stock values from S16 15:45.
Until package A models those gates as divider-plus-mux, clk_set_rate is
a no-op on them; a failure is logged and the bring-up carries on,
because the boot rates already carried a working download.

The binding travels with the driver here instead of in its own patch:
this series is applied as a unit, and splitting it would leave one half
describing hardware nothing reads.

---
diff -Nur a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp.yaml	2026-09-08 18:22:42.130717687 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/sound/allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Allwinner H713 MSP audio DSP
+
+maintainers:
+  - HY310 Mainline Port <hy310@example.invalid>
+
+description: |
+  The MSP is the Trident audio DSP of the H713. It sits on the demodulator
+  bus next to CIP and the demux, takes the HDMI receiver's I2S stream, runs
+  it through its module graph and hands it to the internal codec over
+  I2SOUT1. Software only loads its patch and switches the input, the volume
+  and mute, so the driver registers a control-only ALSA card and no PCM
+  device.
+
+  The block is reachable only while the demod bus clock and reset are on and
+  the TVFE router at 0x06700000 has been written; that router word is shared
+  with the TV top controller, so it is referenced as a syscon rather than
+  claimed as a register range of this node.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp
+
+  reg:
+    items:
+      - description: DSP mailbox, 0x06144000
+      - description: audio top clock control, 0x0614a000
+      - description: audio control block, 0x06142000
+      - description: AUDIF, 0x06146000
+
+  reg-names:
+    items:
+      - const: mailbox
+      - const: audio-top
+      - const: ctrl
+      - const: audif
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 17
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: bus-demod
+      - const: adc
+      - const: dtmb-120m
+      - const: tvfe-1296m
+      - const: i2h
+      - const: cip-tsx
+      - const: cip-mcx
+      - const: cip-tsp
+      - const: tsa-tsp
+      - const: cip27
+      - const: cip-mts0
+      - const: audio-cpu
+      - const: audio-umac
+      - const: audio-ihb
+      - const: tsa432
+      - const: mpg0
+      - const: mpg1
+
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  reset-names:
+    items:
+      - const: bus-demod
+
+  power-domains:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: the TVFE domain the audio island lives in
+
+  allwinner,tvfe-router:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Syscon over the TVFE router word at 0x06700000. The driver reads it as
+      a gate check and writes the value that opens the audio path.
+
+  firmware-name:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: patch image for the DSP, default "h713/msp-patch.bin"
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - reg-names
+  - clocks
+  - clock-names
+  - resets
+  - reset-names
+  - power-domains
+  - allwinner,tvfe-router
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun50i-h713-ccu.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/reset/sun50i-h713-ccu.h>
+
+    audio-dsp@6144000 {
+        compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-msp";
+        reg = <0x06144000 0x20>, <0x0614a000 0x10>,
+              <0x06142000 0x80>, <0x06146000 0x90>;
+        reg-names = "mailbox", "audio-top", "ctrl", "audif";
+        clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_DEMOD>, <&ccu CLK_ADC>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_DTMB_120M>, <&ccu CLK_TVFE_1296M>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_I2H>, <&ccu CLK_CIP_TSX>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_CIP_MCX>, <&ccu CLK_CIP_TSP>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_TSA_TSP>, <&ccu CLK_CIP27>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_CIP_MTS0>, <&ccu CLK_AUDIO_CPU>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_AUDIO_UMAC>, <&ccu CLK_AUDIO_IHB>,
+                 <&ccu CLK_TSA432>, <&ccu CLK_MPG0>, <&ccu CLK_MPG1>;
+        clock-names = "bus-demod", "adc", "dtmb-120m", "tvfe-1296m",
+                      "i2h", "cip-tsx", "cip-mcx", "cip-tsp",
+                      "tsa-tsp", "cip27", "cip-mts0", "audio-cpu",
+                      "audio-umac", "audio-ihb", "tsa432", "mpg0",
+                      "mpg1";
+        resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_DEMOD>;
+        reset-names = "bus-demod";
+        power-domains = <&ppu 1>;
+        allwinner,tvfe-router = <&tvfe_router>;
+        firmware-name = "h713/msp-patch.bin";
+    };
diff -Nur a/sound/soc/sunxi/Kconfig b/sound/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/Kconfig	2026-09-08 17:59:35.565252014 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/Kconfig	2026-09-08 18:19:56.137654496 +0200
@@ -63,6 +63,26 @@
 	  Say Y or M to add support for the DMIC audio block in the Allwinner
 	  H6 and affiliated SoCs.
 
+config SND_SUN50I_H713_MSP
+	tristate "Allwinner H713 MSP audio DSP"
+	depends on SND
+	depends on OF
+	depends on (ARM64 && ARCH_SUNXI) || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on MFD_SYSCON
+	help
+	  Say Y or M to add support for the MSP audio DSP of the Allwinner
+	  H713, the block the HDMI receiver's audio runs through on its way
+	  to the internal codec.
+
+	  The driver brings the audio island up, loads the DSP patch over
+	  the mailbox, builds the HDMI-to-speaker graph and registers an
+	  ALSA card that carries only the three controls that path needs --
+	  input switch, volume and mute. There is no PCM device: nothing
+	  streams through the CPU.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
+	  be called sun50i-h713-msp.
+
 config SND_SUN8I_ADDA_PR_REGMAP
 	tristate
 	select REGMAP
